{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been feeling nauseous and vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, since last night. I had dinner like normal, but then I started feeling sick and threw up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Did you notice any blood in the vomit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It looked kind of like coffee grounds. Is that bad?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:27:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That can mean there’s some irritation or bleeding in the stomach or esophagus. Given your history of gastroparesis and diabetes, this isn’t uncommon during a flare-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had anything to eat today. My stomach just feels full and heavy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:28:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’re going to start you on IV fluids to rehydrate you and give you some anti-nausea medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:29:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Should I still take my insulin even though I’m not eating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:30:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. You must never skip your insulin, even if you're not eating. We’ll adjust the doses based on your blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I’ve been worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve ordered some blood tests and a chest X-ray to make sure there’s no infection or other issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a chest X-ray before, right? For the last admission?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:33:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and this one looks similar—no pneumonia or pneumothorax. Your heart size is normal, and the gastric pacer leads are still in place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, very good. We also did an abdominal X-ray. It shows your bowels aren’t blocked, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been admitted a few times for this. Is this just another flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It looks like a gastroparesis flare, yes. We’re giving you your usual metoclopramide and adding compazine for nausea control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve heard sometimes people make themselves throw up. I don’t do that, just so you know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you for saying that. We just need to understand all possibilities. Your labs show mild dehydration and slightly high white blood cells, but no infection so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my blood pressure? It’s usually high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2197-05-02 11:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a bit elevated today—167 over 84. We’ll keep an eye on it. Your lisinopril dose may be adjusted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2197-05-03 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2197-05-03 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. I didn’t vomit last night, but I still don’t feel like eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2197-05-03 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We’re going to try starting you on small sips of ginger ale and see if you can tolerate toast later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2197-05-03 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My mouth is still dry, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2197-05-03 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing IV fluids to help with that. Your blood sugar has been stable, which is helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2197-05-03 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a urine test last night. Was there anything wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2197-05-03 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It showed mixed bacteria, but that’s likely from contamination. No sign of a urinary infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2197-05-03 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I was worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. You kept down toast and applesauce yesterday. We’re going to advance your diet to soft foods today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re getting there. We want to make sure you can keep food and meds down. We’re also adjusting your medications for long-term protection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like what?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing your lisinopril to 7.5 mg daily to protect your kidneys from diabetes damage. And we’re starting a baby aspirin for heart protection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember starting those last time. Are they working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and it’s important to stay on them. We’re also giving you both oral and rectal compazine in case nausea comes back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The rectal one? I’ve never used that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2197-05-04 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s helpful if you can’t keep pills down. It works well for nausea and is safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2197-05-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You’ve had two meals without vomiting. That’s great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2197-05-05 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling more like myself. Can I go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2197-05-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if you continue to do well. We’ll write your discharge orders today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2197-05-05 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I do if I start feeling sick again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2197-05-05 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take the compazine as prescribed. Avoid large meals, soda, or eating too fast. And never skip insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2197-05-05 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if it doesn’t help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2197-05-05 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or come back if you have fever, chest pain, trouble breathing, or severe pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2197-05-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. You’re stable, eating, and taking your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2197-05-06 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll follow up with my clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2197-05-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Make sure you take the pantoprazole daily for your esophagitis. It helps reduce stomach acid and irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2197-05-06 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll start it today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2197-05-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Keep your blood sugar in check—it helps prevent these flares. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2197-05-06 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2197-05-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check-in before discharge. Any nausea now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2197-05-06 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I feel okay. A bit tired, but no nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2197-05-06 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. Remember—small, frequent meals. No skipping insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2197-05-06 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And take the new meds every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2197-05-06 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’re all set. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2197-05-06 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2197-05-06 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—we reviewed your labs and imaging. Everything supports a gastroparesis flare with no complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2197-05-06 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the coffee ground vomit wasn’t serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2197-05-06 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It suggests mild bleeding, likely from esophagitis or a small tear from vomiting. The pantoprazole will help heal that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2197-05-06 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2197-05-06 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your discharge instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2197-05-06 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I think I’ve got it all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2197-05-06 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad you’re feeling better. Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2197-05-06 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2197-05-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check—any questions before you go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2197-05-06 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m good. All set."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2197-05-02 11:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2197-05-06 15:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A patient with Type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis was admitted for a flare characterized by nausea, vomiting, and hematemesis described as coffee-ground material. She was rehydrated with IV fluids and treated with metoclopramide and compazine for nausea control. Her diet was gradually advanced from clear liquids to soft foods as tolerated. Blood glucose was well-managed throughout the stay, and her blood pressure was addressed by increasing lisinopril to 7.5 mg daily. A urine culture showed mixed flora, consistent with contamination, and imaging ruled out obstruction or pneumomediastinum. She was discharged home in stable condition, tolerating oral intake, with new prescriptions for pantoprazole, aspirin, and both oral and rectal compazine for ongoing management.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Gastroesophageal laceration-hemorrhage syndrome",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Other postprocedural status"
    ]
  }
}
